SUMMARY:Snow Country by Yasunari Kawabata
DESCRIPTION:Books That Age Like Wine\n**At an isolated mountain hot spring
 \, with snow blanketing every surface\, Shimamura\, a wealthy dilettante m
 eets Komako\, a lowly geisha. She gives herself to him fully and without r
 emorse\, despite knowing that their passion cannot last and that the affai
 r can have only one outcome. In chronicling the course of this doomed roma
 nce\, Kawabata has created a story for the ages—a stunning novel dense i
 n implication and exalting in its sadness.**
